{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>For</b> in the place of sea-monsters — the mem in place of nun, as in לקץ הימין. The sense: at the bottom of the sea, the place of sea-monsters, and \"darkness of waters\" — this is the shadow of death, by way of metaphor; the witness is ודכאתנו (Psalms 44:20), like the sense of דכים. And some say: in a place where there is no settlement, only sea-monsters and ostriches."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {0 "The lemma under discussion is the phrase כי דכאתנו במקום תנים (Psalms 44:20); Ibn Ezra reads תנים as a variant spelling of תנינים (sea-monsters). The witness text דכים is uncertain; it may refer to a related form or occurrence of the root דכא."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:49.212489830Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}